{"chunk_id": "e04cae714f22", "text": "Kunti secretly meets Karna before the Kurukshetra war and reveals the truth of his birth: he is her firstborn son, fathered by the sun\u2011god Surya, and therefore the eldest of the Pandavas rather than a charioteer\u2019s son. She urges him to join his brothers and reclaim royal honor beside Arjuna. Surya himself confirms her words, but Karna refuses. Bound by loyalty to Duryodhana, who honored and supported him when others scorned him, Karna argues that abandoning the Kauravas now would be dishonorable. Yet he grants Kunti a painful compromise: he will spare Yudhishthira, Bhima, Nakula, and Sahadeva, fighting only Arjuna. Thus Kunti will still have five sons\u2014either Arjuna or Karna will die. The scene highlights Karna\u2019s tragic nobility and the crushing power of duty, loyalty, and fate.\nKunti reveals Karna\u2019s true birth and begs him to join the Pandavas, but Karna refuses out of loyalty to Duryodhana, promising to spare all brothers except Arjuna.\nThemes: hidden parentage, loyalty vs blood, dharma and honor, maternal plea, fate", "vector": [0.007640516851097345, -0.03268812596797943, -0.0002514311345294118, -0.0018719267100095749, -0.006305087357759476, 0.02726667933166027, -0.016476940363645554, 0.006032686680555344, -0.04321210831403732, -0.02071576751768589, 0.016649683937430382, 0.016835713759064674, 0.006856533698737621, 0.016915440559387207, -0.010131989605724812, -0.009427733719348907, 0.04411568120121956, -0.00952739268541336, 0.043717045336961746, -0.026190362870693207, -0.0026492662727832794, -0.011294676922261715, -0.009979179129004478, 0.011653449386358261, -0.02128714509308338, 0.02403772994875908, 0.0165699552744627, -0.025937894359230995, 0.017393803223967552, -0.03731229901313782, -0.017712712287902832, 0.006411390379071236, 0.0018818925600498915, -0.009540680795907974, -0.03226291388273239, 0.011945782229304314, 0.004072727635502815, -0.03162509575486183, 0.006188818719238043, 0.0002123980666510